{"artifact_id":"extract_569149fae603d01793a91946","byte_end":176821,"byte_start":173379,"format_id":"reviewed-html-paragraph-v1","locator":"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.1","original_html":"<p id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Model-dependent results are derived using the PS method for background estimation, with limits set using the <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"S_{\\text{T}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>T</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{\\text{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> distribution in the SR, defined by <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"N\\geq 4\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>\u2265</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N\\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"S&gt;0.1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S&gt;0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, and SVM score <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"&gt;0.63\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.63</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">&gt;0.63</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe background prediction and observed data for the PS method are shown in Fig.\u00a0<a href=\"#Ch0.F8\" title='Figure 8 \u2023 0.9.2 Model-dependent results \u2023 0.9 Results \u2023 A search for microscopic black holes, string balls, and sphalerons in proton-proton collisions at \u221a\ud835\udc60=13\u2062\"ERROR \\TeV\"' class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">8</span></a>, together with the B1 model at <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n=2\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\text{D}}=2\\TeV\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>D</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><mtext class=\"undefined\">\\TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\text{D}}=2\\TeV</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\text{BH}}=10\\TeV\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>BH</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><mtext class=\"undefined\">\\TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\text{BH}}=10\\TeV</annotation></semantics></math> (red) and with <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m8\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\text{D}}=3\\TeV\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>D</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><mtext class=\"undefined\">\\TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\text{D}}=3\\TeV</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id=\"Ch0.S9.SS2.p1.m9\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\text{BH}}=10\\TeV\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>BH</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><mtext class=\"undefined\">\\TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\text{BH}}=10\\TeV</annotation></semantics></math> (blue) as examples of expected signal distributions. No significant deviation in data compared to the expected SM background is observed.</p>","parser_version":"1.0.0","purpose":"RESEARCH","review_status":"PROPOSED","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_hash":"7fadcfce5fce60055ccd817d98d05c9d09e4c759f1691022a0d3f4f7cf2be955","source_id":"cms_paper_v2","source_version":"2604.10732v2"}